I encountered what appears to be a boundary-condition bug in Patch Level 6.
I had entered a room with a doorway in one of its corners.  The configuration
of the room and the corridor looked something like this:

                   #
                   #
                   #
     -------------.#
     |............|#
     |............|#
     |............|
     |............|
     |............|
     --------------

The dog was inside the room.  I left the room by following the path outlined
below by the numbers 1, 2 and 3:

                   #
                   #
                   #
     -------------2#
     |...........1|3
     |............|#
     |............|
     |............|
     |............|
     --------------

Even though I was now out of the room (and, in fact, proceeded to wander about
the dungeon a bit), I was still able to watch the dog move around inside the
room.

If I left the room using the path [1,2,4] or the path [1,2,5] (see next
diagram), the game properly registered me as being out of the room, and the
dog's image promptly disappeared.

                   #
                   #
                   5
     -------------24
     |...........1|3
     |............|#
     |............|
     |............|
     |............|
     --------------
